## 4. What the census did not know: the facade is not one repo

ADR-2608131600 flagged cloud-itonami/kuni-umi as the single \"facade\" — a
registry that shells back out to bb. Reading every converted registry from
origin/main found **five**, in three distinct shapes:

  cloud-itonami/kuni-umi            2/2 entries `[\"bb\" …]`, bb.edn still present
                                    -> CONVERTED (§2)
  etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-tomoshibi 3/3 entries `[\"bb\" …]`, bb.edn DELETED
                                    -> genuinely broken, reported not fixed
  kotoba-lang/webgpu                its 1 registered task is `[\"bb\" \"--classpath\"
                                    …]`, and the task's own :doc tells the reader
                                    to run `bb gen-compute-golden`
  kotoba-lang/kami-isekai-assets    render-test is `[\"sh\" \"-c\" \"cd ../webgpu &&
                                    exec bb …\"]` — knowingly, per its comment
  etzhayyim/root                    3 of 57 (audit:test-health, test:docs-registry,
                                    vitals:joucho)

tomoshibi deserves its own line because it is the one case where I could not
produce a working command and said so in the repo. Two independent faults, and
fixing either alone changes nothing: (a) the registry shells to bb while bb.edn —
which supplied bb's classpath — is deleted, so it dies on
`Could not locate tomoshibi/agent_test…`; and (b) the suite requires
`etzhayyim_organism.sensors.evangelism-gate`, which is NOT at the documented
sibling path — `etzhayyim/root` carries only `20-actors/todoke` on main, and the
namespace is not in `com-etzhayyim-app-organism` either. Its README recorded
18 tests / 48 assertions green; that was true when measured and cannot be
reproduced from the repository as it stands. Both facts are now in the README.

The general lesson matches §2: a facade is not a half-done conversion, it is a
conversion that has not started AND that suppresses the signal that it needs to.
Four of the five would fail on a murakumo fleet node today, where bb is not
installed — they pass here only because this laptop has it.

## Decision

Fix the arity rather than the message, when the message is what a fixed arity
would make true. Convert facades properly rather than re-pointing them. In
documentation, correct what resolves and NAME what does not, in the same place —
never delete a line for a capability that used to exist, and never substitute a
command that has not been run. Where a replacement cannot be produced, say that
in the repository rather than in a report only the author reads.

## Measured versus fixed

Measured: the live 401 before and after; all 41 converted checkouts read from
origin/main; 5 bb-facade registries found (census had 1).
Fixed: the 401's underlying arity (deployed message now true, message TEXT landed
but not deployed — stated plainly above); kuni-umi converted with both masked
defects repaired, 2/2 tasks run; 20 repositories' documentation corrected; 3
previously-empty registries repaired along the way (kisekae 2 tasks, kami-engine
2 tasks), each task run.
Not fixed: network-awai/cloud-itonami and etzhayyim/root documentation; the two
archived repositories; tomoshibi's missing organism dependency; the 4 remaining
bb-facade registries; the 129 port decisions ADR-2608131600 left open.
